<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cisleithania</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cisleithania was the unofficial name of the Austrian half of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">Compromise of 1867</a>, named after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leitha">Leitha</a> River that formed part of the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. It included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> and other lands. Its Hungarian counterpart was known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Transleithania</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cisleithania.jpg" alt="Cisleithania" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ThrashedParanoid and Peregrine981. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Habsburg_Monarchy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
